+<!doctype html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+<meta charset="utf-8">
+<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+<meta name="theme-color" content="#0b1220">
+<title>Terms &amp; Conditions | ChaosHire</title>
+<meta name="description" content="Terms for using the ChaosHire synthetic hiring-audit prototype, including permitted data and responsible-use limits.">
+<link rel="canonical" href="__PUBLIC_ORIGIN__/terms">
+<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/icons/favicon-32.png">
+<link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/chaoshire.css?v=__CSS_VERSION__">
+</head>
+<body>
+<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>
+<header><div><a class="brand-link" href="/">Chaos<span>Hire</span></a><div class="tag">Chaos Simulator for Fair Hiring</div></div></header>
+<main id="main" class="legal-page" tabindex="-1">
+<p class="kicker">Use this demonstration responsibly</p>
+<h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
+<p class="dim">Effective 24 September 2026 · Please review these terms before using the public demo.</p>
+<h2>Purpose and permitted use</h2>
+<p>ChaosHire is an open-source educational prototype for investigating fairness risks in automated hiring decisions. You may explore the built-in synthetic fixtures and upload <strong>synthetic or properly anonymized</strong> decision data you have the right to use. Do not submit real applicant, employee, or other sensitive personal information to the public demo.</p>
+<h2>What the service does not do</h2>
+<p>The scores, counterfactual experiments, mitigation simulations, and release gates are research and engineering aids, not legal advice, an employment decision, a discrimination finding, or a fairness certification. Do not use this public service to make or automatically enforce real hiring decisions. Human review, valid ground truth, and applicable legal advice are required for any production assessment.</p>
+<h2>Shared features and safety</h2>
+<p>An appeal may appear in a public review queue after imperfect automated redaction. An operator-authenticated upload can publish aggregate results and its name to a public history; an anonymous upload is computed and returned to its uploader without publication. You are responsible for avoiding identifying information and for using the service lawfully. Do not attack, flood, impersonate users, bypass rate limits, or attempt to access another party's data.</p>
+<h2>Availability, code, and changes</h2>
+<p>The free demo may sleep, restart, lose ephemeral history, or change without notice. It is provided “as is”, without a promise of accuracy, fitness for a particular purpose, or uninterrupted access. The source code has its own <a href="https://github.com/dommetipavan26-tech/chaoshire/blob/main/LICENSE">license</a>; these site terms do not replace the source license. The maintainer may update the demo or these terms, with an updated effective date.</p>
+<h2>Privacy and contact</h2>
+<p>Read the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for data handling, browser storage, and optional analytics. For safety or privacy questions, consult the <a href="https://github.com/dommetipavan26-tech/chaoshire/security">repository's Security page</a> for private contact instructions; never put personal information in a public issue.</p>
+</main>
+<footer><a href="/">Home</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> · <a aria-current="page" href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a> · Portfolio prototype; synthetic data only.</footer>
+</body>
+</html>
