+# ChaosHire documentation
+
+Start with the [project overview](../README.md). Paths in the guides' command examples
+are relative to the **repository root**.
+
+## Engineering
+
+- [Architecture diagram](engineering/ARCHITECTURE.svg) — browser, API, audits, evidence, and delivery.
+- [Methodology](engineering/METHODOLOGY.md) — metrics, assumptions, and responsible-use limits.
+- [Continuous fairness](engineering/CONTINUOUS-FAIRNESS.md) — experiments and release-gate policy.
+- [scikit-learn integration](engineering/SCIKIT-LEARN-INTEGRATION.md) — decision-adapter example.
+
+## Operations
+
+- [Persistence and privacy](operations/PERSISTENCE.md) — what is stored and for how long.
+- [Monitoring](operations/MONITORING.md) — deployment posture and operational checks.
+- [Release checklist](operations/RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md) — automated gates and owner actions.
+- [Website readiness](operations/WEBSITE-READINESS.md) — privacy, HTTPS, SEO, accessibility, and page-speed checks.
+- [Security policy](../SECURITY.md) — root-level file so GitHub also discovers it.
+
+## Portfolio
+
+- [Case study](portfolio/PORTFOLIO-CASE-STUDY.md)
+- [Evidence and demo script](portfolio/PORTFOLIO-EVIDENCE.md)
+- [Platform engineering](portfolio/PORTFOLIO-PLATFORM.md)
+- [Screenshots](portfolio/assets/) — regenerated by [`scripts/capture_portfolio.py`](../scripts/capture_portfolio.py).
+
+## Planning and history
+
+- [Roadmap](planning/PROJECT-ROADMAP.md)
+- [Task log](planning/TODO.md) — historical entries may mention paths from earlier releases.
+- [Changelog](../CHANGELOG.md) — historical release notes; old paths in past entries are intentional.
+
+## Where code and tests live
+
+- `chaoshire/*.py` retains its public import paths (for example, `chaoshire.metrics`);
+  `backend.py` retains the `uvicorn backend:app` entry point.
+- `chaoshire/web/` contains `index.html` and `static/`. Both ship **inside the
+  Python package**. The routes for `/`, `/static/chaoshire.css`, and `/icons/...`
+  have not changed. Docker copies this directory along with the rest of
+  `chaoshire/`.
+- `chaoshire/artifacts/` contains the pinned trained-model fixture, not generated
+  reports. `examples/` holds the runnable adapter example. In `scripts/`,
+  [`check_build_info.py`](../scripts/check_build_info.py) checks CI facts,
+  [`generate_icons.py`](../scripts/generate_icons.py) writes PWA icons to
+  `chaoshire/web/static/icons/`, and
+  [`probe_xff.py`](../scripts/probe_xff.py) tests proxy rate limiting. Keep root
+  dependency manifests and deployment configuration in place for Docker,
+  Render, pip, and Dependabot.
+- `tests/api/`, `tests/core/`, `tests/infrastructure/`, and `tests/web/` run with
+  `python -m pytest -q`. `tests/browser/` is opt-in because it requires Playwright:
+
+  ```bash
+  python -m pip install -r requirements-browser.txt -r requirements-examples.txt
+  python -m playwright install chromium
+  python -m pytest tests/browser -q
+  ```
+
+See [contributing](../CONTRIBUTING.md) for the default lint and test commands.
